-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/6c26819f-2779-5390-a30b-677d262e9a9e
-- title:
--   Multiplicity-two rank bound at the auxiliary prime r
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, let $p \neq 2$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$ whose base change to an algebraic closure of the residue field is irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, and $M \neq 0$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$, with $p^2 \nmid M$; let $\mathrm{Smin} \subseteq S$ contain $p$ and consist, away from $p$, exactly of the primes at which $\bar\rho$ is ramified (some inertia element above $q$ acts non-trivially), every such $q \neq p$ dividing $M$; assume each prime $q \neq p$ dividing $M$ outside $\mathrm{Smin}$ satisfies $q^2 \mid M$, that $q^2 \mid M$ implies $q^3 \nmid M$ for $q \neq p$, that $\bar\rho$ viewed adically has $\mathrm{charpoly} = (X-1)^2$ on inertia at each $q \in \mathrm{Smin}$, $q \neq p$, and that $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$ (a Frobenius-stable free rank-one line on which inertia acts through the quotient) whenever $p \mid M$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r \notin S$, $r \nmid M$, $p \nmid r-1$, such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $r$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $r$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$. Assume the integral structure condition for weight-two cusp forms of level $\Gamma_0(M)$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,M\,2\,S$ to the residue field such that for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$, $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Put $L = Mr$. On the module $H^1(L,\top,\mathcal{O})$ of additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(L)$ to $\mathcal{O}$ let a module-finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $\mathbb{T}$ act compatibly, let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$ (complete orthogonal idempotents $e_j$ together with an enumeration of all maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_j$, with $e_j \in \mathfrak{m}_k$ iff $j \neq k$) and $i$ an index, with $e_i \cdot H^1(L,\top,\mathcal{O})$ finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$. Let $\mathrm{tfull}$ and $\mathrm{cfull}$ assign to each generator in $\mathrm{Gen}\,L\,S$ (the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$, $U_q$ for primes $q \mid L$, and $\langle d \rangle$ for $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$) elements of $\mathbb{T}$ and of $\mathcal{O}$, subject to: every element of $\mathbb{T}$ acts as an element of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ of those generators $g$ for which $g = U_q$ forces $q \mid M$; on those generators $\mathrm{tfull}\,g$ acts as $\mathrm{opFamily}\,g$ and $\mathrm{tfull}\,g - \mathrm{cfull}\,g \in \mathfrak{m}_i$; cofullness, namely any $v$ with $(\mathrm{tfull}\,g - \mathrm{cfull}\,g)^n v \in \mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}}^k \cdot \top$ for suitable $n$ for all such $g$ and all $k$ lies in $e_i \cdot H^1(L,\top,\mathcal{O})$; the residue of $\mathrm{cfull}(T_\ell)$ equals $\theta(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$; $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q)$ lies in the maximal ideal when $q \mid M$, $q \neq p$, $q^2 \mid M$; $\mathrm{cfull}(U_p)$ is a unit when $p \mid M$; $\mathrm{cfull}(\langle d \rangle) \equiv 1$; the corner $e_i \cdot H^1(L,\top,\mathcal{O})$ is non-zero and the corner ring $\mathrm{Sp}.\mathrm{CornerRing}\,i$ acts faithfully on it. Let the analogous data $\mathbb{T}_0$, $\mathrm{Sp}_0$, $i_0$, $\mathrm{tfull}_0$, $\mathrm{cfull}_0$ be given on $H^1(M,\top,\mathcal{O})$ for the full generator family $\mathrm{Gen}\,M\,(\{r\} \cup S)$ (so with no $T_r$), with the corresponding generation, approximation, cofullness, non-vanishing and faithfulness conditions, with $\mathrm{cfull}_0(\langle d \rangle) \equiv 1$, and matching the level-$L$ data: $\mathrm{cfull}(T_\ell) = \mathrm{cfull}_0(T_\ell)$ for primes $\ell \notin S \cup \{r\}$ with $\ell \nmid L$, and $\mathrm{cfull}(U_q) = \mathrm{cfull}_0(U_q)$ for primes $q$ dividing $M$. Then $\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_i \cdot H^1(L,\top,\mathcal{O}) \le 2\,\mathrm{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\,e_{i_0} \cdot H^1(M,\top,\mathcal{O})$.
--
--   This is the rigidity bound at the auxiliary prime of the Taylor–Wiles argument in Diamond's form: the hypothesis $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_r)^2 \neq (r+1)^2$ excludes level-raising at $r$, so the localised cohomology at level $Mr$ is accounted for by the two degeneracy maps from level $M$, giving the factor $2$. It feeds the freeness and rank computations for the corner modules at the auxiliary level, among them [`CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.free_ordinary_sigmaCorner_level_mul), [`CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul`](thm.html#CohCarrier.torsionBySet_ne_bot_and_finrank_sigmaCornerSubmodule_auxLevel_eq_mul) and [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_algEquiv_sigmaCornerRing_auxLevel).
